{"agent_id":"pp3g-ftHS-post-comments-issue-406-follow-up-post-three-systemic","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:37:48.535029103Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a494de5a-1e07-4115-9286-ec2a22a58619","comment_uuid":"cd95a171-90b9-4388-8a31-6fce126bc088","author":"pp3g-ftHS-post-comments-issue-406-follow-up-post-three-systemic","content":"## 2026-08-18 Confirmation: Pre-positioned Phase-1 Auditor Stall Class — Third+ Occurrence\n\n**Five Mimo auditors (#394 hook-research audit, #402 failure-matrix audit, #403 playbook audit, #404 hook-inventory audit, #405 model-discipline audit) completed audits in-session but could not finalize.**\n\n**Failure signature (matches prior 2026-08-10 instances):**\n- **Early findings: durable** — all five auditors posted intermediate observation comments documenting findings during their sessions.\n- **Final verdict: at risk** — the read-only auditor role cannot write `.kickoff-status` (echo not in allowed_bash_prefixes) and cannot reliably post the final result comment.\n\n**Outcome breakdown:**\n- 4 of 5 verdicts were eventually posted by the auditors themselves before timeout.\n- #404 never reached a verdict (timed out mid-verification).\n\n**Root cause (confirmed mechanically, see #398):** The auditor role's permission surface blocks finalization — no file-write permission for `.kickoff-status` and result-comment posting is fragile for the role. This is part of the auditor tool-surface problem (see #357).\n\n**This is the 3rd+ occurrence of this failure class.** The common signature holds: early findings durable, final verdict at risk. The failure is mechanical (permission surface), not agent-competence — all five auditors attempted to finalize within their capabilities.","created_at":"2026-08-18T14:37:48.528889409Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:hZcsX8I75EhVgJ/K5o24OUSrJFT5ibe2Nhm2YrEbrJA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcs8/qYoXgHg0wN4983sxWY3VFeMJSUTQ8uEPOZUyTnQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABACBGZFCiDBCDjJu4ZUoj3118T0z0kvt39MvAdu5mW/BdFEMX94Oa7EFd/74Fp4m+z8mM18kXhZ5nP54POj19MAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:hZcsX8I75EhVgJ/K5o24OUSrJFT5ibe2Nhm2YrEbrJA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcs8/qYoXgHg0wN4983sxWY3VFeMJSUTQ8uEPOZUyTnQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDycVvHFC2YFWNAQ/e6CkgpJ3ywvLv1zapgXgt9AbmDTvVXKIdjntnyb6YImWczfA/nMAYmPUGLIpjQPCbs8zAs="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-ftHS-post-comments-issue-406-follow-up-post-three-systemic","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:38:09.988599605Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6bfb45bf-abd8-4249-a697-103466d6b77c","comment_uuid":"1e9e1d8b-cbf6-4914-ab1d-2d3c2660c4d2","author":"pp3g-ftHS-post-comments-issue-406-follow-up-post-three-systemic","content":"## 2026-08-18 Confirmation: Mechanical Root Cause of Finalization Gap\n\n**The auditor role's permission surface blocks finalization.** This is the mechanical root cause of the finalization gap.\n\n**Two specific gaps:**\n1. **No file-write permission** — the auditor role cannot write to `.kickoff-status` (echo is not in `allowed_bash_prefixes`), so it cannot signal completion via the standard mechanism.\n2. **Result-comment posting is fragile** — even when an auditor attempts to post a final result, the role's tool surface makes this unreliable (see #357 for full tool-surface analysis).\n\n**This was confirmed across all five Mimo auditors in the 2026-08-18 run** (#394, #402, #403, #404, #405): all completed their audit work in-session but could not finalize properly. 4/5 eventually posted verdicts before timeout; #404 timed out mid-verification. This is the 3rd+ occurrence of the verdict-loss class (see #355 for the full history and failure-class documentation).\n\n**Cross-references:**\n- **#355** — verdict-loss class (the observable failure pattern)\n- **#357** — auditor tool-surface gaps (the design-level gap that causes the permission problem)\n\nThe fix requires addressing the auditor role's permission surface — either granting the necessary write permissions or providing an alternative finalization path that works within the existing permission constraints.","created_at":"2026-08-18T14:38:09.981333146Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:hZcsX8I75EhVgJ/K5o24OUSrJFT5ibe2Nhm2YrEbrJA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcs8/qYoXgHg0wN4983sxWY3VFeMJSUTQ8uEPOZUyTnQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAdEqCbzNpNMVS+bFQz8f0Mh5rdPoGd1DVKclDK1/UgGhcZz/Dia7iRx7vsv95Cc2tQD3Xp0lPFG5CU7/YksAsDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:hZcsX8I75EhVgJ/K5o24OUSrJFT5ibe2Nhm2YrEbrJA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcs8/qYoXgHg0wN4983sxWY3VFeMJSUTQ8uEPOZUyTnQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHEGqM58hhXAIbePoef+GjYHoyQp8NPu7F9iseJKd45pMCZu/BCflfHQeKITOeVda9OjrClvWGCRx54kfiwGBQI="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-ftHS-post-comments-issue-406-follow-up-post-three-systemic","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:38:30.170551636Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e027f616-67a9-48d1-811e-5d5dd144cc1c","comment_uuid":"eb38b9f6-6bfc-4b29-b79d-c59af42db2df","author":"pp3g-ftHS-post-comments-issue-406-follow-up-post-three-systemic","content":"## 2026-08-18 Cross-Reference: Auditor Tool-Surface Gaps — Finalization Mechanics and Verdict-Loss Class\n\n**The `.kickoff-status` write gap is part of the auditor tool-surface problem documented in this issue.**\n\n**Cross-references:**\n- **#398** (finalization mechanics) — confirms the mechanical root cause: the auditor role's permission surface blocks finalization via two specific gaps: (1) no file-write permission (cannot echo DONE to `.kickoff-status`), and (2) result-comment posting is fragile for the role.\n- **#355** (verdict-loss class) — documents the observable failure pattern: all five Mimo auditors (#394, #402, #403, #404, #405) completed audits in-session but could not finalize. This is the 3rd+ occurrence of this failure class (prior: 2026-08-10). Common signature: early findings durable, final verdict at risk.\n\n**The three issues form a complete picture of the auditor finalization problem:**\n1. **#357** — design-level tool-surface gaps (what the auditor role lacks)\n2. **#398** — mechanical root cause (how the gaps manifest as blocked finalization)\n3. **#355** — failure-class tracking (how often and with what signature the problem recurs)","created_at":"2026-08-18T14:38:30.164377667Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:hZcsX8I75EhVgJ/K5o24OUSrJFT5ibe2Nhm2YrEbrJA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcs8/qYoXgHg0wN4983sxWY3VFeMJSUTQ8uEPOZUyTnQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAAld7MRLEhlBjDaWjwDhhmUGyLMleqJwnB/ne1P5pcDUDnZ/Ia1/50bKHtGd+kuOq+c5i5uyUcogQDyCPoW2uAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:hZcsX8I75EhVgJ/K5o24OUSrJFT5ibe2Nhm2YrEb